  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Jsoup\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Jsoup\n       Program: jsoup\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Jsoup/Jsoup.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/jsoup.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Jsoup/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 93\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Jsoup-33\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n2518e92a052d922d81d11e28b8e5205639fed9a7\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2013-10-06 13:46:11 -0700\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\n305\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://github.com/jhy/jsoup/issues/305\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.jsoup.parser.HtmlParserTest::handlesKnownEmptyBlocks\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: expected:<...src=\"/foo\"></script>[<div id=\"2\"><img /><img /></div><a id=\"3\"></a><i></i><foo /><foo>One</foo> <hr /> hr text <hr />] hr text two> but was:<...src=\"/foo\"></script>[&lt;div id=2&gt;&lt;img /&gt;&lt;img&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;a id=3 /&gt;&lt;i /&gt;&lt;foo /&gt;&lt;foo&gt;One&lt;/foo&gt; &lt;hr /&gt; hr text &lt;hr&gt;] hr text two>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.jsoup.parser.HtmlTreeBuilder\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Self-closing script tag causes remainder of document to be html-escaped.\nState: closed\n\nDescription:\nWhen a self-closing script block is encountered it appears that the state transitions do not account for the closing tag, so the rest of the document is considered to be in the body of the script tag, and so is escaped.\n\nThe unit test HtmlParserTest.handlesKnownEmptyBlocks() will fail if a self-closing script tag is included in the String h.\n\nComments:\n\n[jhy]: Thanks for the report. That's a bit weird.\n\n[jhy]: The problem is that the unexpected self-closing tag handler (which is out of spec) is not getting the Tokeniser out of the ScriptData state. I don't want to just force it back into the Data state, because that ignores other internal states. Probably the right thing to do is track the previous Tokeniser and TreeBuilder states in the emit() method, and transition to those on read().\n\n[jhy]: On review, I think it's OK to force back to state=data. It's explicitly a self closing tag, and could only have got into that state via the data state.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.jsoup.parser.HtmlTreeBuilder (buggy)\n+++ org.jsoup.parser.HtmlTreeBuilder (fixed)\n@@ -159,6 +159,7 @@\n         if (startTag.isSelfClosing()) {\n             Element el = insertEmpty(startTag);\n             stack.add(el);\n+            tokeniser.transition(TokeniserState.Data); // handles <script />, otherwise needs breakout steps from script data\n             tokeniser.emit(new Token.EndTag(el.tagName()));  // ensure we get out of whatever state we are in. emitted for yielded processing\n             return el;\n         }"
